{"id": "EUVD-2026-86128", "enisaUuid": "8b4b1545-fcc9-36f1-aefe-67b060dc10a1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: hibernate: mask DAIF before restoring hibernated kernel\n\nThe arm64 hibernate code manages the exception masking in an unsound\nway, leading to potential crashes and/or warnings during resume.\n\nWhen a hibernation image is saved in `swsusp_arch_suspend()`, all DAIF\nexceptions are masked (by virtue of `local_daif_save()`), and the\nsuspended image is saved assuming that all DAIF exceptions will remain\nmasked when the image is restored.\n\nWhen a hibernation image is resumed by `swsusp_arch_resume()`, only\ninterrupts are masked (by virtue of `local_irq_disable()` in\n`resume_target_kernel()`). When pseudo-NMI is enabled the DAIF.IF bits\nwill be clear, and regardless of pseudo-NMI the DAIF.DA bits will be\nclear.\n\nThis means that there are two problems:\n\n(1) It is possible to take Debug, SError, or pseudo-NMI exceptions\n    during the resume process. This is unsafe, as during the resume\n    process both the old ane new kernels will tranisently be in an\n    inconsistent state, and swsusp_arch_suspend_exit() won't retain\n    an executable mapping of any exception vectors.\n\n    Any exception taken here will be fatal and silent.\n\n(2) When re-entering the resumed kernel, some DAIF bits will be clear\n    unexpectedly. This permits Debug, SError, or pseudo-NMI exceptions\n    to be taken for a short period while the resumed kernel is not yet\n    in a consistent state.\n\n    This is detected by CONFIG_ARM64_DEBUG_PRIORITY_MASKING.\n\nAvoid these issues by masking all DAIF exceptions during resume.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:51:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:08:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9c671e9ab87b639720db8f7f8648bdf0f3bc8ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/099ad3edcef1d955d9f5d6aab16ae78ecdfd4cda", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/716c41bd476334afb943308be9ff2142e34461b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5370853041a3cb53a125b77528586278f64b378b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/290c5b0c9fc0c61fb1c41421ed2394f955206ea0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/012823494e20c3cce622982ebd3fd6971be39ad2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d736ace2c491623c9ab5e73744085e93e9ae3ebe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/684bde100117931f4c51c644a95f42f2dab041bc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93256", "GHSA-jf3q-gp4f-qwvj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "28653375-9cdb-3ff3-a6ac-de27e68d67da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82869ac57b5d3b550446932c918dbf2caf020c9e <684bde100117931f4c51c644a95f42f2dab041bc"}, {"id": "315375d7-1583-3fbb-920e-13ab2d2ef9f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "32399fb5-a9ff-389d-b8a7-bcc303f49b5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82869ac57b5d3b550446932c918dbf2caf020c9e <d736ace2c491623c9ab5e73744085e93e9ae3ebe"}, {"id": "41072ec0-555e-3aa1-b624-a33f818eef24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "519eb964-7a2e-3fab-b3f4-e907867be7b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "54cb9051-86b3-344a-bb36-77c977d5b522", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.7"}, {"id": "60341ea4-1480-30e6-a67d-19be32352cbe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82869ac57b5d3b550446932c918dbf2caf020c9e <c9c671e9ab87b639720db8f7f8648bdf0f3bc8ec"}, {"id": "630146e3-594b-3ea8-8649-520be45eda2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "84ec4b05-3abe-3903-9973-b2c6f558873a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82869ac57b5d3b550446932c918dbf2caf020c9e <716c41bd476334afb943308be9ff2142e34461b7"}, {"id": "a40eda73-239b-3252-8972-78eee26441f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82869ac57b5d3b550446932c918dbf2caf020c9e <099ad3edcef1d955d9f5d6aab16ae78ecdfd4cda"}, {"id": "b1f8ee7f-2b25-3ece-8c57-55156e9c430c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "b4daf1fd-aa4e-3b80-aa17-741216b71cf4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82869ac57b5d3b550446932c918dbf2caf020c9e <5370853041a3cb53a125b77528586278f64b378b"}, {"id": "db2dab6a-fbd7-3c7f-9775-34c485cb61d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "db977813-dcaf-3d36-bf2b-eb57a10d0d74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82869ac57b5d3b550446932c918dbf2caf020c9e <012823494e20c3cce622982ebd3fd6971be39ad2"}, {"id": "e1a23366-6103-30e6-b1b9-25adb7878178", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e6674112-3482-3081-94f5-b23cca8cfc1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "f2ea3902-0b75-3db7-8afb-02dd7b4257b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82869ac57b5d3b550446932c918dbf2caf020c9e <290c5b0c9fc0c61fb1c41421ed2394f955206ea0"}, {"id": "fcf931f0-9948-3222-a20b-77ef5a02e8b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9a0580d7-2494-3614-b350-278cde086e74", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}